WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.320
The entity that is SCP-4840-A&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:09.680
is an old man who calls himself the caretaker&nbsp;
of the floating city of Audapaupadopolis.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:14.720
He holds secrets that will change the&nbsp;
Foundation’s understanding of the world forever.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:20.240
The old man was initially encountered by Captain&nbsp;
Francis Pike who first explored Audapaupadopolis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:27.040
for the Foundation. It was here that SCP-4840-A&nbsp;
provided some insight into the city and its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:34.640
mysteries. Over a decade later, the Foundation has&nbsp;
sent Dr. Val Ostrovich to interview the old man.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:40.720
Unbeknownst to her, everything she and everyone&nbsp;
else thinks they know, is about to change.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:45.440
SCP-4840-A walks into the&nbsp;
room where Dr. Ostrovich sits.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:48.320
“Please take a seat,” she says to the old man.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:53.440
He looks around at the barren stone walls and&nbsp;
takes a few steps into the center of the room.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.280
Dr. Ostrovich motions to the&nbsp;
chair across the table from her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:00.480
The old man pulls the chair out and takes a seat.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:05.280
Dr. Ostrovich leans over and pushes a button&nbsp;
on the voice recorder resting on the table.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:09.360
“That’s very impressive,” the old&nbsp;
man says, examining the device.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.840
“So, it records everything I say?”

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:14.880
“That is correct,” responds Dr. Ostrovich.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:20.720
The old man looks around the room and then&nbsp;
directly into her eyes. A smile cracks his lips.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:25.840
“I wondered when the Foundation&nbsp;
would want to talk… like actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:30.960
talk. You are a seeker of knowledge.&nbsp;
You reminded me a little of my brother;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:36.400
he may have been the greatest scholar that ever&nbsp;
lived. And now you seek the truth. For that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:40.480
we will need to take a journey&nbsp;
billions of years into the past.”

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:42.880
“Billions?” asks Dr. Ostrovich.

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:47.280
“Billions,” the old man answers,&nbsp;
folding his hands on the table.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:53.520
“I was there from the beginning.” The old man&nbsp;
begins to tell his tale. It is so vividly worded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:59.120
that Dr. Ostrovich feels like she is living&nbsp;
in the story; like she’s been transported to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:05.040
a different time and place to experience the&nbsp;
creation of the universe and the fall of man.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:12.240
In the beginning, there was light. The iron god&nbsp;
manifested itself; his sword cut flaming stars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:18.080
into the sky. The god of flesh sprinkled drops&nbsp;
of blood onto the earth creating the first life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:23.520
The Serpent of sin and its Dark Brother laid&nbsp;
the foundation for what is and what is not.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:28.320
A young boy looked up at the sky as&nbsp;
the Earth began to turn. He watched&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:34.880
the creation of everything from the Great Hall of&nbsp;
Audapaupadopolis. This was where humans were born.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:39.200
“Wait, I don’t understand,” says&nbsp;
Dr. Ostravich. “Are you telling me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:42.080
that Audapaupadopolis is like the Garden of Eden?”

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:48.000
“I am not telling you that it is like anything.”&nbsp;
the old man says with a wink. “But I think you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:52.720
want to learn more about a different&nbsp;
tale. Something I will get to in time.”

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:58.880
In the early days of the universe, there were only&nbsp;
a few humans in existence. For millions of years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:04.160
they watched through the haze of creation to learn&nbsp;
more about the reality they were born into. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:10.560
built the very first city and upon completion, it&nbsp;
became the spot where that which IS came to be.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:19.360
There were only ever two true gods: IS and IS NOT.&nbsp;
They were the only truths in the entire universe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:24.400
IS brought the Serpent into the world. It&nbsp;
searched for whence it came and to learn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:31.120
about all the truths that had been hidden from&nbsp;
it. The IS NOT was the darker shadow of IS.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:35.840
It controlled everything that stretched&nbsp;
out beyond the world and into the unknown.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:39.360
The two gods could not exist without one another.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:42.720
“When you refer to the Serpent do&nbsp;
you mean the entity that resides in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:45.920
the Wanderer's Library?” interjects Dr. Ostravich.

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:49.200
“One and the same,” replies the old man.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:54.960
It was during the time after the IS and IS NOT&nbsp;
finished creation that the monsters and demons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.960 --> 00:04:01.360
inhabited the Earth. However, there was order;&nbsp;
the monsters of other worlds were kept separate.

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:07.040
These entities would be in the dreams of men but&nbsp;
were never able to cross over to their world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:10.800
It was the strange folk to the&nbsp;
west of Audapaupadopolis that first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:16.240
opened their eyes to the cosmos. They were&nbsp;
created from the last remnants of the IS,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:21.040
but were not human; they were something&nbsp;
that could not be explained by logic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:26.960
The humans were looked after by the mothers of&nbsp;
the newly created world. The wolf, the bear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:32.480
the sow, and the lion were their protectors.
As the days went on more and more men&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:37.920
and women walked the streets of Audapaupadopolis.&nbsp;
They met in the Great Hall of the city where they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:44.000
would seek counsel and listen to the First King of&nbsp;
Men. His name was Asem, which came from the word&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:50.800
that meant “IS.” His skin looked as if it was&nbsp;
made of gold and he had power beyond imagining.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:54.960
Although Asem was only a man, he could&nbsp;
create mountains with his hands and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.960 --> 00:05:00.240
deep oceans with his feet. He had a&nbsp;
lance that could kill even the gods.&nbsp;

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:05.040
Asem was a great leader, but deep&nbsp;
inside of him grew the first vice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:10.640
of man—envy. He would look to the&nbsp;
heavens and desired them to be his.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:17.840
Humans had built the greatest city that would ever&nbsp;
be, and yet, the king wanted more—so he took it.

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:22.400
Asem was the first being to seize something&nbsp;
from a world that was not his own.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:26.720
He stole a crown. And when he gathered&nbsp;
the inhabitants of Audapaupadopolis to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:32.960
the Great Hall to show them his new relic,&nbsp;
he declared himself the King of All That IS.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:37.040
He built his seat of power on top of&nbsp;
the spot where mankind first found&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:43.280
IS. Asem was still kind to the people of&nbsp;
Audapaupadopolis, but he always desired more.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:49.040
Then the great betrayals came. Asem’s sons&nbsp;
grew up in the shadow of their father’s envy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:53.680
The first betrayal was by his middle&nbsp;
son who coveted his father’s crown.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:58.000
He demanded that it be passed on&nbsp;
to him, and when Asem refused,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:02.640
the son amassed an army and laid siege to&nbsp;
the world. But the middle son was struck&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:08.240
down by his father and locked in a stone tomb&nbsp;
deep under the grounds of Audapaupadopolis.

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:13.520
The second betrayal came from Asem’s oldest&nbsp;
son. He went behind his father’s back and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:18.720
spoke passionately to the people using sense&nbsp;
and reason to demand that they make his father&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:24.960
give him the crown. The people of the Earth&nbsp;
worshiped Asem’s oldest son as if he were a god.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:30.000
Seeing this, Asem removed the poison that&nbsp;
his eldest son had put into their minds.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:34.240
He then dealt with him by casting his&nbsp;
son to the most desolate place on Earth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:38.080
where he would wander until&nbsp;
the sun went down in the east.

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:42.400
The most devastating betrayal of all&nbsp;
came from the youngest son of Asem.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:47.680
He came into his father’s bedroom while he slept&nbsp;
and took the crown from his head. The youngest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:53.440
son and his followers ran away with the crown.&nbsp;
When Asem awoke, his heart broke with what his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:59.440
youngest son—whom he loved more than anyone&nbsp;
or anything in the entire world—had done.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:05.360
An endless rage welled up in the king and he&nbsp;
turned the Earth into a smoking wasteland.

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:11.360
Asem searched tirelessly for his youngest&nbsp;
offspring and the crown. His envy knew no bounds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:15.920
and he desired nothing more than for&nbsp;
his crown to be returned to him. For&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:20.320
thousands of years Asem searched but&nbsp;
could not find what he was looking for.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:24.880
The crown had been hidden away&nbsp;
and slowly faded into legend.

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:30.400
The world gradually returned to normal. Fields&nbsp;
began to regrow, and forests sprouted from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:36.000
smoldering embers of the planet-wide siege that&nbsp;
Asem had carried out in search of his crown. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:41.920
followers of his youngest son spread across the&nbsp;
region, which would later become known as Europe.

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:48.480
Then came the time of endless wars. Men fought&nbsp;
demons and monsters; men fought one another.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:53.120
From these wars came the deaths of many and&nbsp;
the ancient ruins that have long since been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:59.200
consumed by the sands of the Earth. But these wars&nbsp;
would lead to the current age of human history.

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:04.080
During the great wars, one man hid and watched&nbsp;
from the Great Hall at Audapaupadopolis.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:08.240
He witnessed the world consume&nbsp;
itself. But the worst was yet to come.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:13.280
Xorus the Sky King found his way to&nbsp;
Audapaupadopolis and demanded that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:17.920
be given the lance of Asem. However,&nbsp;
the lance had been lost long ago&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:22.880
with the fall of the First King of Man as&nbsp;
he ravaged the planet looking for his crown.

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:28.400
Xorus refused to believe the lance was not in&nbsp;
the city and began to destroy Audapaupadopolis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:32.800
as he looked for it. But before Xorus&nbsp;
could completely demolish everything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:38.320
a hidden mystery was called upon to&nbsp;
stop the threat. The last of the titans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:43.440
the great dragon Bharath who slumbered&nbsp;
beneath the city, emerged from the Earth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:49.680
and carried Audapaupadopolis into the sky.&nbsp;
Forever separating it from the men of the world.

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:53.600
“You mean until the Foundation&nbsp;
discovered it,” says Dr. Ostravich.

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:58.800
“Well… yes and no,” replies the old&nbsp;
man. “There was one before you.”

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:02.880
The history of man progressed. Daeva&nbsp;
hero of Gilgamesh killed Sarrus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:07.840
II's only son in single combat on the&nbsp;
fields of Jerusalem. The dreaded sorcerer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:12.880
Noah El Mehtoh flooded the lands until&nbsp;
he was killed by Malidrau the Wrathful.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:17.840
Jorei Apollyon sailed across the great sea&nbsp;
to meet with the king of the Night Children&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:24.480
but was buried alive to feed the heart of their&nbsp;
tree goddess. Then, from the east, came Lancelot.

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:28.880
“Like the knight from King Arthur’s Knights&nbsp;
of the Round Table?” asks Dr. Ostravich.

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:32.240
The old man frowns. “No, that&nbsp;
was a different Lancelot. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:37.120
one who came to the floating city&nbsp;
was called the Demon Lancelot.”

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:40.080
As the Demon Lancelot approached Audapaupadopolis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:45.440
any remaining allies who still walked the Earth&nbsp;
were called upon for assistance. The evil army&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:50.800
that the demon commanded would not be easily&nbsp;
defeated. Lancelot first targeted Bharata,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:56.160
the old dragon who had lifted Audapaupadopolis&nbsp;
into the skies, next he battled the sea lord&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.160 --> 00:10:02.320
Arkthurus, he made quick work of the hero&nbsp;
Beowulf, and lastly fell the King of David.

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:08.080
All that remained between the Demon Lancelot&nbsp;
and the city of Audapaupadopolis was one human.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:14.080
He took up his sword and battled the demon, but&nbsp;
Lancelot was too strong. The demon used the flails&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:18.960
attached to his six arms to demolish anything&nbsp;
in his path. He was about to land the deadly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:24.800
blow when with its last breath, the dragon Bharata&nbsp;
ripped the Demon Lancelot’s heart out of his chest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:30.000
and cast him into the Temple of Sunset&nbsp;
where his dead body lies to this day.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:35.520
All was now quiet in Audapaupadopolis.&nbsp;
The gods and heroes of old had been lost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:41.200
or were hidden away. The search for the crown&nbsp;
continued on and even Asem himself is somewhere&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:47.280
scouring the Earth for his precious relic. The&nbsp;
floating city of Audapaupadopolis was forgotten.

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:51.360
“So, basically most of the SCPs&nbsp;
that the Foundation contains come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:54.560
straight from your history,” Dr. Ostravich says.

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:59.760
“Yes, I believe you are correct,” replies the old&nbsp;
man. “Just from this story alone, there must be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:06.000
entities you recognize. And the fact that many of&nbsp;
the gods, early men, and demons are immortal means&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:12.160
you will probably hear more about them in time.&nbsp;
The Demon Lancelot may seem dead, but his body&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.160 --> 00:11:18.560
still radiates heat; I feel it is only a matter&nbsp;
of time until we must do battle once again.”

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:24.720
“There is something I don’t understand,”&nbsp;
Dr. Ostravich says. The old man nods at her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:28.960
“Where do you fit into this story? I&nbsp;
understand you were there at creation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:32.960
but you know so much, and I can’t help&nbsp;
but feel you are leaving something out.”

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:41.280
The old man pauses. He lets out a long sigh.&nbsp;
“My name is Seth,” the old man says. “Brother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.280 --> 00:11:49.600
to Cain and Able, son of Adam El Asem… the First&nbsp;
King of Men. I was the King’s youngest who stole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:56.640
the crown. I was the one who looked at the night&nbsp;
sky and asked my father for a star all my own.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.640 --> 00:12:03.200
He pulled one out of the heavens for me and it&nbsp;
became the iron crown. It drove my father to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:10.720
madness, my brothers to butchery, and led to the&nbsp;
ruination of our kingdom. The crown is the seed at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.720 --> 00:12:18.080
the root of all evil.” Seth stares blankly across&nbsp;
the room. “And it was meant as a gift for me.”

00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:22.320
Now watch “SCP 073 &amp; 076 - Cain vs Able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:28.160
(SCP Animation).” Or check out&nbsp;
“SCP-343 - God (SCP Animation).”

